"""Buys for one shopper inside an ORO store world.

Built on the public YesYesYes v1 agent, itself built on the public Know Thyself v1 and KYO v6 agents. It takes parts of the
public Halo v2 agent and rebuilds ideas from the public Cooler Man v7 agent in its own code. A light model walks the store with the world's
own tools; code keeps the ledger, questions the shopper and stops wasted steps; a heavy model reads the request and
checks the cart before an order and the evidence before a decline.

Changes YesYesYes v1 made to Know Thyself v1, kept here:
- The heavy model stops a little earlier in an episode's spending, to stay clear of the per-run inference cap.
- A heavy model at its request limit hands the call to the next of its kin at once instead of waiting.
- A decline is reviewed against the request and the shopper's answers: requirements that only repeat the story are
  set aside, values that picked up connecting words are corrected, and new searches run before the second look.
- A stated answer is read again by the heavy model, so its value reaches the ledger exactly.
- No re-asking with example values; with very few messages, only properties most listings carry are asked about.
- A cheapest pick lists cheaper rows itself before checkout: through a category listing under a price limit where the
  store has one, else through keyword searches that combine the required values with other values listings show.
- Two requested products on one shelf are merged only when their quantities agree.

Changes from YesYesYes v1:
- An effort count from steps, model sends, stalled calls and backoff decides when exploring stops. Store calls have a
  fixed timeout and a counted retry with backoff.
- Compatibility is read from code-shaped tokens alone: hyphenated codes, whole series, exceptions, a part's series.
- Steps are kept back until a first ending was tried once the cart is full, since a refused ending can need a swap and
  another try. A refused decline counts as a try too.
- Listing price and stock fields are learned on the first search, whatever the pick rule.
- Every ending follows one rule in code: a complete cart that no line's own record contradicts is ordered, a cart with an
  empty line is not, and a cart line stays until its replacement is in. Before an order each line gets a facts read. A
  refused cancel is judged again under the new limits, and long episodes cart what states every need before turns run out.
- A chain of pages starts when it becomes known, not at checkout. A page counts as read only when a read showed its note,
  and the tool that shows notes is learned from the store's own records. A chain ends on a page that sends nothing further.
- With several products, pages are read round robin until each has three before the first question. A reply is filed under
  the product it names, a one-at-a-time reply moves on to the next planned property, and a stated property is not asked
  again under a close name.
- Store records sent as text stay out of the note reader, and reads are counted per call.
"""
